{"BuildIndex no longer takes b.cacheMu.Lock() around the build, allowing multiple callers to enter BuildIndex for the same key concurrently and each create and flush a separate index before the last writer wins in the map": 0.9185348749160767, "TotalDocs() method iterates b.cache without any lock, increasing the chance of concurrent map access during reads when combined with the unlocked build path": 0.8535347580909729, "Loop variable capture in search.init: the closure passed to group.Go references info directly, and since the range variable is reused across iterations, every goroutine can observe the same final info value unless copied per-iteration, causing concurrent initialization to build the same namespace/resource multiple times and skip others": 0.18125231564044952, "NewResourceServer now calls s.Init(ctx) synchronously during construction instead of deferring initialization, meaning any failure in lifecycle init, search index rebuild, or watcher startup now aborts server creation entirely with no retry path since Init is guarded by sync.Once": 0.9228989481925964, "Update returns nil, ErrOptimisticLockingFailed directly when resource version check fails instead of returning a non-nil response with rsp.Error populated, altering the RPC contract and potentially breaking optimistic-lock retry logic": 0.08751150965690613, "Init is now executed from NewResourceServer using a synthetic context (context.Background()) instead of a request-scoped context, which can tie initialization work and watcher creation to the wrong lifecycle if startup takes long or hooks assume request-derived cancellation/trace context": 0.3479451537132263, "Stop() does not terminate the search watcher goroutine started during Init because that watcher was started from context.Background(), so canceling s.ctx cannot reach it, leaving the background search-index consumption loop alive after shutdown": 0.8945239186286926, "NewUninitializedSearchServer comment still says the returned search server must be initialized later and init can be deferred, but this is misleading since NewSearchServer immediately calls Init(context.Background()) and NewResourceServer now eagerly initializes during construction": 0.019268441945314407, "NewUninitializedResourceServer comment is stale as it describes deferred initialization as the standard lifecycle, but NewResourceServer now eagerly invokes Init and request handlers no longer call it": 0.05976944789290428}